==English==

===Etymology===
''[[fanny]]'' (British colloquial slang for a ''[[vagina]],'' not a fanny or rear-end) + ''[[fart]]'' (emission of a gas.)

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[fanny]] [[fart]]}}

# {{British|slang}} A noise made by the emission of air from the [[vagina]], usually associated with a physical activity such as [[horse riding]] or [[intercourse]].
# {{US|mildly vulgar|or|baby talk}} A (normal) [[fart]].